{{!
    @template tool_vae/declaration

    One claim, drawn for reading: a definition list of its lines, then the narrative under its heading.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\declaration. The template holds no logic. Every
    label and value is escaped (double braces). One key is HTML (triple braces): situationhtml, the narrative passed
    through format_text() of the core with the format the vaeiste chose (plain text or Markdown).

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * rows - array of {label, value}: the lines of the claim, as plain text
    * situation - string, the heading of the narrative
    * situationhtml - HTML, the narrative

    Example context (json):
    {
        "rows": [
            {"label": "Record", "value": "RNCP36832-C03"},
            {"label": "Competency", "value": "Spot the risk factors of a fall"}
        ],
        "situation": "Situation",
        "situationhtml": "<div class=\"text_to_html\">Help with getting up.</div>"
    }
}}
<dl class="tool-vae-claim">{{#rows}}<dt>{{label}}</dt><dd>{{value}}</dd>{{/rows}}</dl>
<h3>{{situation}}</h3>
<div class="tool-vae-situation">{{{situationhtml}}}</div>
